1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:04,950
Vienna, 1791. Salieri poisons Mozart.

2
00:00:05,100 --> 00:00:07,583
Nope. No evidence at all.

3
00:00:07,733 --> 00:00:09,783
Mozart and Salieri: the poison myth.

4
00:00:09,933 --> 00:00:12,783
Mozart died at 35.

5
00:00:12,933 --> 00:00:15,183
After weeks of illness.

6
00:00:15,333 --> 00:00:18,550
Doctors at the time blamed a fever.

7
00:00:18,700 --> 00:00:22,150
Nobody knows exactly what it was.

8
00:00:22,300 --> 00:00:24,917
But poison? No sign of it.

9
00:00:25,067 --> 00:00:28,583
And Salieri wasn't a jealous loser.

10
00:00:28,733 --> 00:00:31,750
He was the emperor's top composer.

11
00:00:31,900 --> 00:00:35,117
He taught Beethoven, Schubert and Liszt.

12
00:00:35,267 --> 00:00:37,950
He even taught Mozart's son.

13
00:00:38,100 --> 00:00:41,183
The two of them wrote a piece together.

14
00:00:41,333 --> 00:00:44,483
It was found again in 2016.

15
00:00:44,633 --> 00:00:47,183
So where did the poison come from?

16
00:00:47,333 --> 00:00:50,283
Gossip in Vienna, years later.

17
00:00:50,433 --> 00:00:54,417
Then a play by Pushkin. Then the movie Amadeus.

18
00:00:54,567 --> 00:00:57,283
A great story. Not history.

19
00:00:57,433 --> 00:01:01,150
Proof Salieri poisoned Mozart: zero.

20
00:01:01,300 --> 00:01:05,117
Anyway, here's Salieri with his poison.
